        hero: "./assets/images/guild.webp", heroAlt: "Turing Guild growth path", heroCaption: "Organizational growth from parties to regional coordination networks.",
        content: `<section><h2 id="guild-growth">Growth</h2><ol class="flow-list"><li><b>Party</b><span>Stable coordination around adventure, PVP, and resources.</span></li><li><b>Guild</b><span>Roles, treasury, missions, distribution, and member rules.</span></li><li><b>Regional network</b><span>Bases, events, markets, education, and real-world activity.</span></li><li><b>Ecosystem work</b><span>Public works, content, and DAO groups across Guilds.</span></li></ol></section><section><h2 id="guild-tools">Tools</h2><div class="feature-grid"><div class="feature-card"><h3>Members and roles</h3><p>Terms, approvals, and actions remain queryable.</p></div><div class="feature-card"><h3>Shared missions</h3><p>Work, proof, progress, and rewards are defined in advance.</p></div><div class="feature-card"><h3>Resources</h3><p>Treasuries, bases, land, and tools use limits and audits.</p></div><div class="feature-card"><h3>Proposals</h3><p>Internal governance leads to ecosystem participation.</p></div></div></section><section><h2 id="healthy-referrals">Healthy referrals</h2><p>Node referrals follow the node-page rules. After game launch, player referrals follow the two-level 7% / 2% consumption-reward rules on the Player Referral Rewards page. No third or deeper level is counted, and recruitment is never required to access core gameplay.</p></section>`
