        content: `<section><h2 id="core-functions">Core functions</h2><div class="feature-grid"><div class="feature-card"><h3>Product and game design</h3><p>World, systems, balance, content cadence, and research.</p></div><div class="feature-card"><h3>Client and server</h3><p>Multi-platform experience, game services, matching, data, and reliability.</p></div><div class="feature-card"><h3>Blockchain and security</h3><p>Contracts, wallets, indexing, nodes, markets, audits, and response.</p></div><div class="feature-card"><h3>Art and world building</h3><p>Characters, environments, animation, VFX, UI, and creator standards.</p></div><div class="feature-card"><h3>Economy and data</h3><p>Tokens, revenue pools, stress tests, dashboards, and risk.</p></div><div class="feature-card"><h3>Community and business</h3><p>Guilds, market agents, brands, events, support, and coordination.</p></div></div></section><section><h2 id="decision-rights">Accountability</h2><p>Product owns scope, technology owns architecture and security, economy owns parameters and disclosure, and community owns communication and appeals. Asset and node decisions retain written review trails.</p></section><section><h2 id="team-disclosure">Disclosure plan</h2><p>Before public fundraising, asset sales, or mainnet launch, the project should publish verified names, roles, experience, conflicts, vesting, and official contacts. Unconfirmed advisors or investors are never listed.</p><div class="callout"><p>This page describes the organization and does not invent biographies. The named team list will follow identity and authorization checks.</p></div></section>`
